  "result": "Perfect! All 109 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added VAT calculation:\n   - Imported `roundCents` from money.js\n   - Added `lineVAT(line)` \u2014 calculates VAT on the line amount **after discount**, rounded per line\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n   - Invoice VAT = sum of all rounded line VATs\n\n2. **src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to display VAT:\n   - Shows \"VAT: \u20acX.XX\" line when VAT > 0\n   - Positioned just above the total line\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 15 comprehensive VAT tests covering:\n   - lineVAT with and without discounts\n   - lineVAT with different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n   - invoiceTotals with VAT\n   - VAT rounding behavior\n   - Invoice VAT = sum of line VATs\n   - Complex scenarios with discounts + VAT\n   - VAT from actual catalogue products\n   - All updated existing tests to include VAT field\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- VAT is calculated per line on the post-discount amount\n- VAT is rounded per line, never a percentage of the invoice total\n- Invoice VAT is the sum of these rounded per-line VAT amounts\n- All monetary amounts are clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\nAll 109 tests pass successfully.",
